# Migration rehearsal log (MUSE-004, 2026-10-03)

## Method

Live PG17 apply was attempted and sandbox-blocked (evidence below), so
the rehearsal ran statically at full depth instead:

1. Parsed all 19 Studio migration files with the real PostgreSQL
   grammar (libpg_query via pglast 8.4): **19/19 files, 0 syntax
   errors, 726 top-level statements.**
2. Per-statement idempotency audit: IF (NOT) EXISTS / OR REPLACE /
   DROP-then-create pairing / guarded DO blocks / ON CONFLICT. 677
   statements proven replay-safe by rule; 49 flagged and each confirmed
   by reading the surrounding code (all are `CREATE POLICY` without a
   preceding drop — first apply succeeds, replay aborts).
3. Prereq extraction from the in-file `STUDIO_V5_*_PREREQ` gates plus a
   full non-`studio_v5` reference scan: hard deps are `public.projects`,
   `public.tenants`, `public.project_members`,
   `public.is_project_member(uuid)`, roles `authenticated/service_role`,
   extension `pgcrypto`, and 15 legacy backfill-source tables.
4. Backfill review: every apply-time `perform studio_v5_j*_backfill()`
   is resumable (legacy-map PK skips + `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`;
   j13 is validation-only) and writes only `studio_v5_*` tables.
5. Authoritative DDL for every prereq/legacy object was read in the
   monolith migrations and encoded as `seed.sql` (27 statements, parses
   clean); `apply.sh` reproduces the intended live run for MUSE-009/CI.

## Live-server attempts (all blocked by the sandbox, none by the repo)

- `initdb` (Homebrew PG 17.11): fails — the sandbox blocks directory-
  service user lookup (`could not look up effective user ID`).
- Booting a byte-copy of the initialized PG17 data dir from /tmp over a
  unix socket (no TCP): postmaster dies on `shmat: Operation not
  permitted` — the sandbox denies SysV shared memory.
- Docker: not installed. `require_escalated` shell: denied (no human
  approver in this session). Loopback TCP listen: EPERM.
- No production/staging database was touched (forbidden in this job).

